# international phonetic alphabet

// also includes extIPA, APA and UPA.
//
// should only include: i) a group of inter-related IPA characters;
//                     ii) unicameral characters in use with IPA.
// if casing is introduced later, that character should go elsewhere
// because some languages are definitely using them in everyday setting.
// put a comment `// also IPA` for the design consistency in this case.

